  "created": "2022-04-13T02:31:46.271Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As of now, proximity receivers will give you the distance between the **contact sender** and the **contact receivers center**. \n\nI desire the ability to flip the logic, where we could choose to get the distance from the **contact senders center** to the **contact receiver.**\n\nThis is needed for cross-avatar interaction where we need to know the size of the sender object or require a normalized value that would not be affected by the senders scale.\n\nBelow I have added 2 gifs to better demonstrate. Treat the sphere and the knife as *separate* avatars.\n**Purple** - This is the current system. A contact receiver will measure the distance between the receivers center and the colliding contact sender.\n**Orange** - This is my desired system. Being able to measure from the contact receiver to the center of the contact sender. This makes the senders scale matter.\n\nThe logic is the same for both, just inverse of what we have now.\n\nnakos",
